<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Smart Grid Interface Protection System</title>
    <style>
        @page { size: A4; margin: 0; }
        .page {
            width: 794px; height: 1123px;
            padding: 50px 60px; box-sizing: border-box;
            overflow: hidden; page-break-after: always;
            position: relative;
            font-family: "DejaVu Serif", "Liberation Serif", Georgia, "Helvetica", Arial, sans-serif;
        }
        .page:last-child { page-break-after: auto; }
        h1, h2, h3 { font-family: "DejaVu Serif", "Liberation Serif", Georgia, "Helvetica", Arial, sans-serif; }
        .header-logo { font-family: "DejaVu Sans", "Liberation Sans", Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 48px; }
        .section-title { font-weight: bold; font-size: 18px; margin-bottom: 10px; }
        .body-text { font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.6; }
        .diagram-container { text-align: center; margin: 40px 0; }
        .table-header { font-weight: bold; }
        .footer { position: absolute; bottom: 50px; width: 100%; font-size: 10px; color: #555; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="page">
        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-bottom: 40px;">
            <div>
                <h2 style="font-size: 14px; color: #555; margin-bottom: 5px;">SMART GRID</h2>
                <h1 style="font-size: 36px; margin: 0;">Smart Grid Interface<br>Protection System</h1>
                <h3 style="font-size: 20px; margin-top: 5px;">Next level solutions</h3>
            </div>
            <div class="header-logo">ABB</div>
        </div>

        <div class="diagram-container">
            <!-- Placeholder for the main system diagram -->
            <div style="border: 1px solid #ccc; padding: 20px; background-color: #f9f9f9;">
                <!-- Visual representation of the system components -->
                <p style="font-size: 10px;">[System Diagram Placeholder]</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-top: 50px;">
            <div style="width: 48%;">
                <h3 style="font-size: 14px; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 10px;">01</h3>
                <p class="body-text"><span data-field="component_name_01">{{ component_name_01 }}</span></p>
                <h3 style="font-size: 14px; font-weight: bold; margin-top: 30px;">02</h3>
                <p class="body-text"><span data-field="component_name_02">{{ component_name_02 }}</span></p>
                <h3 style="font-size: 14px; font-weight: bold; margin-top: 30px;">03</h3>
                <p class="body-text"><span data-field="component_name_03">{{ component_name_03 }}</span></p>
            </div>
            <div style="width: 48%;">
                <div class="body-text">
                    <p>Embedding microgrid protection in a single device with <span data-field="component_name_embed">{{ component_name_embed }}</span>, <span data-field="component_name_embed_2">{{ component_name_embed_2 }}</span> & <span data-field="component_name_embed_3">{{ component_name_embed_3 }}</span> Interface Protection System (IPS).</p>
                    <p>The connection of active users to Utility network is subject to local standards requirements. In particular, A unit of power generation such as solar or wind generation that is installed in user's plant shall be disconnected from the grid whenever the voltage and frequency values of the grid itself are out of range specified by standard.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="page">
        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 40px;">
            <div style="width: 48%;">
                <h3 style="font-size: 14px; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 10px;">02</h3>
                <p class="body-text">[Diagram Placeholder]</p>
                <h3 style="font-size: 14px; font-weight: bold; margin-top: 30px;">01</h3>
                <p class="body-text">[Diagram Placeholder]</p>
            </div>
            <div style="width: 48%;">
                <div class="body-text">
                    <p>Such disconnection is usually carried out by an Interface Device that trips after receiving an opening command sent by an external Interface Protection System.</p>
                    <p>With <span data-field="component_name_combo">{{ component_name_combo }}</span> and <span data-field="component_name_combo_2">{{ component_name_combo_2 }}</span>, ABB designed a unique integrated solution which embeds both functions of Interface Protection System (IPS) and Interface Device (ID).</p>
                    <p>Moreover, with <span data-field="component_name_combo_3">{{ component_name_combo_3 }}</span> you can take advantage of the same functionalities even if various circuit breakers - either by ABB or by other manufacturers - are installed in your system.</p>
                    <p>This advanced feature is possible thanks to the implementation of several interface protections into <span data-field="component_name_feature">{{ component_name_feature }}</span> installed on board of low-voltage circuit breakers and built-in inside <span data-field="component_name_feature_2">{{ component_name_feature_2 }}</span> or <span data-field="component_name_feature_3">{{ component_name_feature_3 }}</span> digital units.</p>
                    <p>Today, the embedded IPS is suitable for the connection of active users as specified by main Standards.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="page">
        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 40px;">
            <div style="width: 48%;">
                <div class="section-title">Benefits</div>
                <div class="body-text">
                    <p>Thanks to <span data-field="component_name_benefit_1">{{ component_name_benefit_1 }}</span> and <span data-field="component_name_benefit_2">{{ component_name_benefit_2 }}</span> with embedded Smart Grid Interface Protection System, the following benefits are guaranteed:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Space saving in switchboards and a more compact solution. Installation of an external relay is no longer necessary.</li>
                        <li>If <span data-field="component_name_benefit_3">{{ component_name_benefit_3 }}</span> or <span data-field="component_name_benefit_4">{{ component_name_benefit_4 }}</span> are installed on the generator feeder, the circuit breaker is able to perform triple function of Interface Protection System, Interface Device and Generator Device thanks to the Interface Protection System embedded into the <span data-field="component_name_benefit_5">{{ component_name_benefit_5 }}</span>.</li>
                        <li>Ease of use, thanks to <span data-field="component_name_benefit_6">{{ component_name_benefit_6 }}</span> software which allows an immediate and intuitive commissioning phase.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div style="width: 48%;">
                <div class="section-title">Application examples</div>
                <div class="body-text">
                    <p>Thanks to the embedded functions integrated in a single device, the number of components to be installed is reduced, with consequent space saving inside the switchboard. <span data-field="component_name_app_1">{{ component_name_app_1 }}</span> and <span data-field="component_name_app_2">{{ component_name_app_2 }}</span> are suitable to fully satisfy the requirements of the following scenarios:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>In existing plants, <span data-field="component_name_app_3">{{ component_name_app_3 }}</span> enables interface protection system as a plug & play solution in a wide range of plant size. <span data-field="component_name_app_4">{{ component_name_app_4 }}</span> units share the same electronics of circuit breakers to satisfy all market opportunities of metering, protections and control in power distribution and generation.</li>
                        <li><span data-field="component_name_app_5">{{ component_name_app_5 }}</span> or <span data-field="component_name_app_6">{{ component_name_app_6 }}</span> as microgrid main circuit breaker.</li>
                        <li>In such scenario, with a power of tens/hundreds of kVA and hundreds of kVA/some MVA flowing through <span data-field="component_name_app_7">{{ component_name_app_7 }}</span> and <span data-field="component_name_app_8">{{ component_name_app_8 }}</span> respectively, these circuit breakers can fulfill the double function of Interface Device and Interface Protection System. In case of IPS tripping, the low-voltage microgrid downstream of the main circuit breaker remains active thanks to both the local generation and the load shedding feature embedded in the main circuit breaker (either <span data-field="component_name_app_9">{{ component_name_app_9 }}</span> or <span data-field="component_name_app_10">{{ component_name_app_10 }}</span>).</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="page">
        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 40px;">
            <div style="width: 48%;">
                <div class="section-title">Functions available</div>
                <div class="body-text">
                    <h4 style="font-weight: bold; margin-top: 20px;">Voltage protections</h4>
                    <p>Overvoltage (ANSI 59) with double threshold S1, S2 - Function trips when the phase voltage exceeds the set thresholds.</p>
                    <p>Undervoltage (ANSI 27) with double threshold S1, S2 - Function trips when the phase voltage falls below the set thresholds.</p>
                    <p>Voltage restrained</p>
                    <p>Maximum zero-sequence voltage (ANSI 59 V0) - Function is tripped when the zero-sequence voltage exceeds the set threshold.</p>
                    <p>Maximum negative-sequence voltage (ANSI 59 V0) - Function trips when the negative-sequence voltage exceeds the set threshold.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div style="width: 48%;">
                <div class="section-title">Diagrams</div>
                <div class="diagram-container">
                    <!-- Placeholder for Voltage Protection Diagram -->
                    <div style="border: 1px solid #ccc; padding: 20px; background-color: #f9f9f9;">
                        <p style="font-size: 10px;">[Voltage Protection Diagram Placeholder]</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="diagram-container" style="margin-top: 30px;">
                    <!-- Placeholder for Frequency Protection Diagram -->
                    <div style="border: 1px solid #ccc; padding: 20px; background-color: #f9f9f9;">
                        <p style="font-size: 10px;">[Frequency Protection Diagram Placeholder]</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="page">
        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 40px;">
            <div style="width: 48%;">
                <div class="section-title">Frequency protections</div>
                <div class="body-text">
                    <p>Overfrequency (ANSI 81H) with double threshold S1, S2 - Function trips when the frequency exceeds the set thresholds.</p>
                    <p>Underfrequency (ANSI 81L) with double threshold S1, S2 - Function trips when the frequency falls below the set thresholds.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div style="width: 48%;">
                <div class="section-title">ROCOF (ANSI 81R)</div>
                <div class="body-text">
                    <p>Function trips when the rate of change of frequency exceeds the set threshold.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="section-title" style="margin-top: 30px;">RQ (ANSI 40/32R)</div>
                <div class="body-text">
                    <p>Function trips when the reverse reactive power exceeds the set threshold.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="page">
        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 40px;">
            <div style="width: 48%;">
                <div class="section-title">System Architecture Diagram</div>
                <div class="diagram-container">
                    <!-- Placeholder for the full system architecture diagram -->
                    <div style="border: 1px solid #ccc; padding: 20px; background-color: #f9f9f9;">
                        <p style="font-size: 10px;">[Full System Architecture Diagram Placeholder]</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div style="width: 48%;">
                <!-- Empty space or summary -->
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="page">
        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 40px;">
            <div style="width: 50%;">
                <div style="font-size: 14px; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 10px;">ABB Australia Pty Limited</div>
